\newlabel{tbl-occ-trends}{{5}{17}{Dynamic Occupancy}{table.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Estimated occupancy trends for seven bat species in Southeast Alaska (2017--2025) from a dynamic occupancy model. Trend slope is the average annual change in the proportion of sites occupied (e.g., 0.03 = +3 percentage points per year). λ is the net change in the proportion of sites occupied from 2019 to 2025 (e.g., 0.23 = 23 percentage points higher in 2025). Values are posterior means with 95\% credible intervals. P(increase) is the proportion of posterior draws in which occupancy was higher in 2025 than in 2019; values near 0.5 indicate no clear direction, and values near 1 or 0 indicate stronger evidence of an increase or decline. Bold rows indicate trend slopes and λ whose 95\% credible interval both exclude zero.}}{17}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
