\newlabel{fig-cov-occupancy}{{4}{18}{Covariate effects on initial occupancy, colonization, persistence, and detection probability for each species, modelled using combined data from Alaska and British Columbia. Because Alaska contributes less than 10\% of the data, these effects mainly reflect patterns in the British Columbia dataset. Effects whose 95\% confidence intervals do not overlap zero are shown in colour (blue for positive, red for negative); all others are shown in grey}{figure.caption.6}{}}
